          en: 'He flies off the deck to face [[donquixote-doflamingo|Doflamingo]] alone and buy the ship the minutes it needs. Doflamingo slips the first two kicks and blocks the third, and grants that it was a strong one; then the strings take him and leave him hanging in the air with nothing of his own to move. He tells [[nami|Nami]] and [[brook|Brook]] to leave him there and go. The blow meant to kill him is already coming when [[trafalgar-law|Law]], watching from the shore, throws a log, trades his own place for it in mid-air, and pulls him out of the way.',
